WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:10.320
I'm Councillor Paul Williams from the Waimakariri District Council and I'm here to

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.839
tell you a few of the facts that's
happened from the wrap up of the

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.280
November council meeting.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.480
We've approved
funding for the Southbrook main trunk

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:27.800
line that's coming into Rangiora
from the South Brook sewage system to

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:34.880
improve the capacity of the sewerage for Rangiora.  The councillors decided to

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.270
organise this over the school holidays, so there was not so much disruption to the

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.800
Southbrook schools and preschool in
the area.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.600
The Council passed the adoption of the
Waimakariri Accessible Strategy and

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:55.719
this will give wee bit more access for
disabled people around Waimakariri and

00:00:55.719 --> 00:01:01.909
improve hopefully quite a lot of the
problems they're having in the area so

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.680
that's been passed in this council
meeting which is a good thing.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.800
The council have deferred payments for the
Riding For The Disabled, which the

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:18.200
Council has loaned them some funds
to buy prefab unit for the club rooms

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.880
and they've now deferred the payments so
the club have a wee bit more time to

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.369
make payments to the council to
2020, so council looking after them as

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:31.040
best we can.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:37.830
In 1892 there was a gravel pit area
that was designated for the local

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:44.940
council then, and the Waimakariri Council
now have just gone invested that as a

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:52.470
reserve for utilities which will give a
position to put a new water bore for

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:56.840
Oxford community for the future planning
of Oxford.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.360
So that was a bit of a wrap-up

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.600
what's happened on this particular
council meeting in November and the

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.050
biggest meeting, probably of the year, is
going to be coming up in December where

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:11.069
some of the real nitty gritty important bits and pieces will be brought up.

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:16.470
I believe the four courts and the
three-bin system will be discussed on

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:22.080
that time so that will be interesting to
look forward to.

